@saolence/dsh-restart-handoff README · 一句话：改完插件、装完工具，DSH（DeepSeek Harness）常会说一句「需要重启才生效」。手动重启意味着：关掉窗口、重新打开、自己回想刚才做到哪，再把需求重打一遍。

这个插件把这段空档填上：重启前把交接话写到磁盘，重开之后它作为新会话的第一条消息出现，模型照着往下做。**一个任务要重启五次，就续五次，中间不断线。**

它不改造你的模型，也不联网——只在本机读写几个状态文件。

@saolence/dsh-restart-handoff README · 它不会添乱的几个地方：- **等所有窗口都空下来**——不只是当前会话，子任务和别的窗口也在等，避免重启时把别人的回答掐掉。
- **不会连环重启**——两次重启之间至少隔 60 秒；一次重启只续跑一次，交接话最多投递 3 次。
- **拒绝时说清原因**——冷却期内点重启，界面会说「刚重启过，再等 42 秒」，而不是假装正在重开。

@saolence/dsh-restart-handoff README · Introduction：<p align="center"><img src="icon.svg" width="84" alt="dsh-restart-handoff"></p>

<h1 align="center">dsh-restart-handoff</h1>

<p align="center"><strong>An auto-restart plugin for DeepSeek Harness Desktop and <code>dsh web</code> hosts: when a change only takes effect after a restart, it restarts the host for you and hands "why we restarted, what to do next" back to the same session — restart as often as you like, the task never loses the thread.</strong></p>

@saolence/dsh-restart-handoff README · Four moments you will use it：Editing a built-in tool, editing host code, restarting over and over to run tests — each round comes back carrying the previous round's progress, so the request never has to be restated.

**4. You just want the new build now**

Settings → "Restart handoff" → "Restart now". This one only restarts; it does not auto-resume.

@saolence/dsh-restart-handoff README · Where it stays out of the way：- **It waits for every window** — not just the current session: subagents and other windows count too.
- **It will not loop** — at least 60 seconds between restarts; one resume per restart; a hand-off note is delivered at most three times.
- **It says why when it refuses** — tapping restart inside the cooldown tells you "restarted just now, wait 42 more seconds" instead of pretending it started.

@saolence/dsh-restart-handoff README · Install：> Match the profile to the host you run: `desktop` for the app, `web` for `dsh web`. Installed into the wrong one, the plugin does nothing.
>
> Editing this package does **not** hot-reload: the profile points at it through a symlink, so HMR never hears about the change. Toggle the plugin off and on (or restart once) after editing.

@saolence/dsh-restart-handoff README · Also works with `dsh web`：- **A fresh browser tab opens.** `dsh web` mints a new access token on every boot, so the old tab is always stale; the plugin watches the new process for the printed address and opens it. Close the old tab.
- **It has to be launched from a terminal.** The plugin records its own command line and replays it after exiting. If a process manager (systemd, pm2) owns the host, leave automatic restart off and let the manager do it.
- **With `--no-open` no browser is opened**; the new address is written to `~/.dsh/restart-handoff/cli-host.log`.
